<DocsLayout
  title="About"
  description="Font.Garden is a US-based AI lab for typography: open fonts, open-weight models and the NeuralType font format."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <div class="chapter-introduction">
      <p>
        Font.Garden is a US-based AI lab rethinking typography for global
        scripts. We are developing NeuralType, a post-OpenType font format in
        which every font is a neural network. We train and release open-weight
        vector graphics models, with paid API access to our frontier models.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/fonts/">Fonts</a>: FTGD-100, an index of one hundred free
        and open source fonts. Each font has the same specimen page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/models/">Models</a>: open-weight models that draw glyph
        outlines, and fonts in the NeuralType format.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/docs/">Documentation</a>: the guide to the source files,
        the design rules, the build, the checks and the training data.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Position</h2>
    <p>
      The collection has no named authors. The fonts have the SIL Open Font
      License 1.1, without a Reserved Font Name. The model weights have the
      Apache-2.0 license. The training data comes only from the sources of
      the collection. See
      <a href="/docs/culture/">Post-authorship and open weights</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Source code</h2>
    <p>
      The font sources, the tools and this website are at
      <a href="https://github.com/fontgarden">github.com/fontgarden</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Open an issue in a repository of
      <a href="https://github.com/fontgarden">github.com/fontgarden</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
